keywords:
  - measurement uncertainty
  - ISO/TS 20914
  - Nordtest TR 537
  - external quality assessment
  - internal quality control
  - analytical performance specification
  - clinical chemistry
abstract: >-
  Single-file, offline application that computes the measurement uncertainty of a
  clinical measurement procedure from internal quality control and external quality
  assessment data under nine published top-down model formulations, exposes the four
  conventions the guidance leaves open as separate settings, and classifies each model
  as applicable, conditional or not applicable from the type of assigned value of the
  laboratory's EQA scheme. Distributed with the verification scripts that reproduce the
  worked examples of the source documents and an independent re-implementation.
